target: internal/learn/learn.go
verify: go test ./internal/learn/ -count=1 -run 'TestLearnMatchesThePython/bump_'
expect: --- FAIL:
why:    bump re-dates the ONE entry the caller judged a re-match. A substring is loose, so re-dating every entry containing it would refresh unrelated entries and keep them from ever aging out.
--- old
			lines[i] = "- " + today + ": " + m[2]
			return true
--- new
			lines[i] = "- " + today + ": " + m[2]
